                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like the game's idea.\r\n\r\nFinally, a golfing game where you're not THE golf ball but can actually walk around (and interact a bit with the world, even though, being honest, it's pretty lame here). \r\nEven the collectibles aren't located in the cool spots.\r\n\r\nAnd I genuinely had fun playing this game, even when replaying the courses multiple times.\r\nIt's basic, but it's enjoyable, and at least it's not overdoing it.\r\n\r\nIt's such a shame it's so unpolished, though.\r\n\r\nFor how few gameplay mechanics it has, a lot of them have bugs and technical errors. \r\nThere are basically no settings (only volume control, which doesn't even seem to work). \r\nSome very basic gameplay mechanics aren't present either, like checking your overall score using a dedicated key (you have to finish a hole for it to show up).\r\n\r\nThe music, however, is very nice, albeit it might just be some royalty-free generic one, and the game does look good, although most of it might just be asset flips.\r\n\r\nA fun little game to kill some time.",
